<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf Duala Manga Bell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1873–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf Duala Manga Bell was king of the Bell people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douala">Douala</a> in German Kamerun. Educated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, he led legal resistance to the colonial plan to expropriate Duala land along the river, petitioning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a>. Accused of treason, he was hanged by the Germans in August 1914 and is honoured as a national hero in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-duala-manga-bell.jpg" alt="Rudolf Duala Manga Bell" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rudolf_Manga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
